          <span class="nur-seo__num">01</span>
          <h3>Your skin assessment</h3>
          <p>The app maps fine lines, texture, redness and acne from your answers to the questionnaire and, if you choose, a selfie. That assessment becomes your baseline. Skincare products in use, treatments in progress and retinoids are declared in the same step.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="nur-seo__card">
          <img class="nur-seo__card-img" src="{{ 'nur-skincoach-step-2-weekly.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="700" loading="lazy" alt="Nur Skincoach app on a phone: the weekly routine with LED sessions, focus, skincare pairing and progress against the baseline">
          <span class="nur-seo__num">02</span>
          <h3>Your personalised routine, week by week</h3>
          <p>Each week the app returns your routine: wavelengths, order, frequency, and the skincare products to pair. The routine is read before the session and followed as written; frequency is not raised on a separate decision. Progress is read against the user's own baseline.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="nur-seo__card">
          <img class="nur-seo__card-img" src="{{ 'nur-skincoach-step-3-wavelengths.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="700" loading="lazy" alt="Nur Protocol face mask, neck panel and controller with the seven LED wavelengths">
          <span class="nur-seo__num">03</span>
          <h3>Personalised routine versus standard routine</h3>
          <p>LED masks are usually compared on wavelength, LED count, session length and price. On most of them, the programme is chosen by the user and stays fixed. NŪR Protocol adds a step: your routine is set from your assessment and adapted every week.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="nur-seo__row">
    <div class="nur-seo__label"><span class="nur-seo__idx">The light</span><h2>What each of the seven wavelengths does</h2></div>
