    <div class="nur-seo__faq">
    <details class="nur-seo__faq-item">
      <summary><h3>How often is NŪR Protocol used, and does NŪR Skincoach set the frequency?</h3><span class="nur-seo__plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>NŪR Protocol does not follow one standard routine for everyone. The frequency, the wavelength combination and the skincare products to pair are set in NŪR Skincoach, which builds your personalised routine from your skin assessment (a short questionnaire, plus a selfie if you choose) and adapts it as your skin changes. The user manual recommends 3 to 5 sessions a week, in 4-week cycles; sessions follow the routine shown in the app, and frequency is never increased on your own initiative.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="nur-seo__faq-item">
      <summary><h3>Can NŪR Protocol be used with a retinoid (retinol, tretinoin, adapalene)?</h3><span class="nur-seo__plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>Retinoids such as retinol, tretinoin and adapalene can leave the skin more reactive, so this FAQ does not set the combination. Any retinoid in use is declared during the NŪR Skincoach assessment so that your routine accounts for it, and the sequence is confirmed with the prescribing dermatologist before the first session. The session stops if irritation appears.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="nur-seo__faq-item">
      <summary><h3>What precautions apply to the eyes?</h3><span class="nur-seo__plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>The LEDs are never looked at directly. Two silicone eye protectors are included and, as the user manual describes, are put in place before the mask is switched on. The user manual advises against the device for people with a hereditary eye condition; for any other eye condition, recent eye surgery or particular sensitivity, ask an ophthalmologist before use. The device does not treat eye conditions.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="nur-seo__faq-item">
      <summary><h3>Can NŪR Protocol be used during pregnancy or breastfeeding?</h3><span class="nur-seo__plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>No. The user manual rules out pregnancy and breastfeeding, and NŪR Skincoach does not offer a routine during these periods.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="nur-seo__faq-item">
      <summary><h3>From what age can NŪR Protocol be used?</h3><span class="nur-seo__plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>NŪR Protocol is a skincare device for adults, intended for people aged 18 and over.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="nur-seo__faq-item">
      <summary><h3>Is the neck panel used at the same time as the mask?</h3><span class="nur-seo__plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>Yes. The face mask and the neck panel both plug into the same controller, with the Y adapter cable included, and run during the same session.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="nur-seo__faq-item">
      <summary><h3>What does the NŪR Skincoach assessment change in practice?</h3><span class="nur-seo__plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <p>The assessment (a short questionnaire, plus a selfie if you choose) maps fine lines, texture, redness and blemishes, then turns them into a personalised routine: which of the seven wavelengths to combine, in which order, how often and with which skincare products. NŪR Skincoach records this first assessment as your starting point, so your progress is measured against your own skin, not an average.</p>
    </details>
    </div>
